No, I don't know of such a list. I only noticed that because shortly
before the tournament I almost lost a tourist to C343-324[1]. Since
then I got an eye open for fatal bugs in vanilla NetHack.


Because for NetHack-De I wanted those crashes fixed I first made a few
patches for vanilla:

Long worm crash bug fix   http://bilious.homelinux.org/?332
Acid dropping bug fix     http://bilious.homelinux.org/?340
Iron bars hitting bug fix http://bilious.homelinux.org/?341

Oh, I just noticed that I forgot to submit one more patch. When a
wielded/swapped/quivered object gets deallocated (like a lit candle
burning out), the programm doesn't correctly clear the corresponding
wield/swap/quiver slot and a crash because of a dangling pointer might
occur.

Until bilious gets updated, the patch can also be downloaded from
http://bhaak.dyndns.org/nethack/nh343-applied-cream-pie-C343-218.diff


On Bilious are more bug fixes, but these "only" fix non-fatal bugs:

Astral call bug fix by me                   http://bilious.homelinux.org/?337
Vanishing Items Bugfixes by Michael Lehotay http://bilious.homelinux.org/?165
Win32 locales by Ray Chason                 http://bilious.homelinux.org/?313 [2]
Zero-turn wrest fix by Bent Dalager         http://bilious.homelinux.org/?329


[1] "Cutting a long worm in two will crash the game if the cut takes
     the worm to 1 HP or if long worms had become extinct." 
[2] But this one is of course not of interest for the tournament code.
